{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788291340,"nonce":"ndftE809f4dxOJjBkKBEi8aIGyY=","title":"1.6 until:{condition|layout}: four branches the acceptance suite never reaches","message":"Filed by the session-19 round itself, unasked, because `accept/fc287ba-until-state.py`\nreturned 140/140 on a live bench and a green number that size reads as coverage\nit does not have. Four branches of the shipped code were never executed by it,\nand NONE of them is a map-luck gap — the suite was run on four different\nquicktest maps and could not have hit any of them by chance.\n\n## What is not tested, and why each one matters\n\n**1. `Materials.Availability.Unreachable`.** Phase 2 proves the forbidden bucket\n(300 WoodLog forbidden -\u003e `short_by: 185`, hint names `unforbid`) and the\ngenuinely-absent bucket (Plasteel, `short_by == needed`, hint says \"genuinely\nshort\"). The THIRD bucket — material that is present and unforbidden and that no\ncolonist can reach — never fired, so the `unreachable` field and its hint have\nnever been produced by a running game. It is the bucket whose fix is neither\n`unforbid` nor mining, which is the whole reason the three are separated.\n\n**2. A `condition` over `colonists.list[*]` with a quantifier.** Every predicate\nthe suite evaluates is `time.hour`, which is nine field reads and measured at\n0.0012-0.0015 ms/frame. `colonists.list[*].mood_pct` costs a `Room.Role` — a\nfull room analysis, DigestVerb's own \"most expensive line in the file\" — PER\nCOLONIST PER EVALUATION. The cost note in StateWatch.cs is a reading of the\nsource, not a measurement, and the one number the spec asks to be measured is\ntherefore measured only on the cheapest path available.\n\n**3. `scan_cap` on the layout scope, and the `unscanned` state token.** A layout\nwith more than 300 live elements is the only way to reach it. The suite's\nlayouts are 4 and 22 elements. So a seventh state token ships unexercised, and\nwith it the claim that `done`/`unresolved` stay exact while only DETAIL is\ncapped.\n\n**4. `unknown` (an evicted placement) and `off_map`.** `Layouts.Progress` counts\na placement id the table no longer holds as RESOLVED — deliberately, so an\nadvance cannot hang on discarded evidence — and `construction {layout_id}` emits\na row saying so. Reaching it needs 2000 placements past `Placements`' cap.\n`off_map` needs a second map. Both are correctness claims with no witness.\n\n## What this is NOT\n\nNot a defect report: nothing here is known to be wrong. It is the difference\nbetween \"140 checks passed\" and \"the surface is covered\", written down so the\nnext reader does not confuse them. RUNLOG session 19 records the same list.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A fixture where the material is present, unforbidden and UNREACHABLE (walled\n  off, or across water) produces a `shortfall[]` row with `unreachable \u003e 0`,\n  `forbidden` absent, and the hint naming a path problem rather than a shortage.\n  `available` excludes it.\n- `advance {until:{condition:{path:\"colonists.list[*].mood_pct\", op:\"\u003c\",\n  value:N, quantify:\"any\"}}}` halts on a colony driven into it, and the\n  advance's own `until.eval_ms_per_frame` is compared against the same figure\n  for a `time.hour` predicate on the same bench. Both numbers are recorded. If\n  the colonist path is more than ~50x the clock path, the default\n  `Config.ConditionScanFrames` is re-argued against that measurement rather than\n  left at 15.\n- A layout of \u003e300 live elements reports `scan_more \u003e 0`, at least one item with\n  `state: \"unscanned\"`, and — the load-bearing half — `done`, `built`,\n  `cancelled` and `unresolved` that are EXACT, checked against a per-placement\n  poll of the same ids.\n- The `unknown` branch is exercised without a 2000-placement run if a cheaper\n  route exists (a `Placements` cap override for the test would be one); if none\n  does, say so on the issue and leave it as a source-reading rather than\n  inventing a fixture that does not reproduce the real path.\n- Zero red errors.","files":null}]}